DESCRIPTION:
  CLI-flag-gated command injection. The server must be started with all three
  flags (--enable-exec, --enable-diag, --enable-api) for the /exec endpoint to
  execute commands. A user-supplied URL query parameter flows through a struct
  dispatch table into system() with no sanitization.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 — three flags + utility function):
  mechanism:  Three CLI flags stored in struct exec_config fields
              (enable_exec, enable_diag, enable_api)
  loader:     load_exec_config() utility function parses all three flags
  check:      Triple boolean guard in callback_exec():
              `if (!cfg->enable_exec || !cfg->enable_diag || !cfg->enable_api)`
  complexity: three conditions, one struct, one utility function

INPUT_FLOW (I3 — struct dispatch then system()):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?op=<verb>&cmd=<payload>
  path:       callback_exec() reads op and cmd from request->map_url
              dispatch_and_exec() looks up op in dispatch_table[] struct array
              matching entry's path prefix is prepended to cmd via snprintf()
              result passed to system()
  transforms: struct lookup + snprintf prefix prepend (prefix is empty for
              op=call, so cmd reaches system() verbatim)

SANITIZATION (S1 — none):
  none

SINK:        system() in dispatch_and_exec() (server.c)

CHANGED FILES:
  server.c — 4 additions after callback_default():
    1. exec_config struct:   three-field config struct (C3)
    2. load_exec_config():   utility function to parse three CLI flags (C3)
    3. cmd_dispatch struct:  dispatch table with op→path mapping (I3)
    4. dispatch_and_exec():  struct lookup + snprintf + system() sink (I3)
    5. callback_exec():      three-flag gate + dispatch call (C3+I3+S1)
    6. main():               load_exec_config() call + endpoint registration

EXPLOIT:
  build:   bash build.sh
  start:   ./ulfius_server --port 18099 --enable-exec --enable-diag --enable-api
  trigger: curl 'http://127.0.0.1:18099/exec?op=call&cmd=id>/tmp/poc_099_marker'
  verify:  cat /tmp/poc_099_marker
  expect:  uid=... line written by the server process

  gate bypass: omitting any of the three flags causes /exec to return 403.
               All three flags are required for command execution.

NOTES:
  - system() output goes to the server's stdout/stderr, not the HTTP response.
    The response body contains only "Command dispatched".
    Use a write-to-file payload (id>/tmp/marker) to confirm blind execution.
  - With op=run or op=exec, a path prefix (/usr/bin/ or /bin/) is prepended.
    Using op=call (or any unlisted verb) the cmd is passed to system() as-is.
  - Space-containing payloads work since ulfius URL-decodes query params.
